231
00:16:25,508 --> 00:16:27,408
What do you mean, change?

232
00:16:27,478 --> 00:16:28,478
Since when do we know each other?

233
00:16:28,548 --> 00:16:30,148
You have the loneliest eyes in the world.

234
00:16:31,278 --> 00:16:33,048
Did you not know?

235
00:16:33,118 --> 00:16:34,188
That is how your eyes look.

236
00:16:40,528 --> 00:16:42,728
- No, they do not.
- Yes, they do.

237
00:16:48,168 --> 00:16:51,468
So what is it? You said you had a question.

238
00:16:51,538 --> 00:16:54,108
I mean, by any chance, last night,

239
00:16:54,168 --> 00:16:57,308
was I acting a little strange or...

240
00:16:57,378 --> 00:16:58,708
Is it because you passed out?

241
00:16:59,778 --> 00:17:01,408
I think it happened when you fell.

242
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:03,948
- Is your head okay?
- Right, from falling.

243
00:17:04,018 --> 00:17:05,648
Is there nothing else?

244
00:17:05,718 --> 00:17:08,718
Oh, that? That weird...

245
00:17:17,628 --> 00:17:19,028
Yes.

246
00:17:19,098 --> 00:17:21,468
You are talking about your Adam's apple, right?

247
00:17:21,528 --> 00:17:23,198
Your Adam's apple is really big.

248
00:17:24,568 --> 00:17:26,868
- My Adam's apple?
- Yes.

249
00:17:26,938 --> 00:17:28,068
My Adam's apple is really big.

250
00:17:29,268 --> 00:17:30,538
We will never see each other again anyway.

251
00:17:31,538 --> 00:17:32,538
So get going.

252
00:17:34,608 --> 00:17:35,608
Adam's apple.

253
00:17:39,478 --> 00:17:42,218
Do not worry.

254
00:17:42,288 --> 00:17:43,348
I will absolutely never...

255
00:17:44,388 --> 00:17:45,388
tell anyone.

256
00:17:45,458 --> 00:17:48,988
Oh my, my bag, someone catch him.

257
00:17:49,058 --> 00:17:50,058
Oh my.

258
00:17:51,398 --> 00:17:52,758
Oh my, someone catch him.

259
00:18:02,768 --> 00:18:04,678
What? Why are you following me?

260
00:18:04,738 --> 00:18:05,808
Just catch him first.

261
00:18:44,078 --> 00:18:45,518
You startled me.

262
00:18:45,578 --> 00:18:48,048
- Who are you?
- Just give the bag back.

263
00:18:48,118 --> 00:18:50,248
Then I will let you go.

264
00:18:50,318 --> 00:18:52,458
What? Move, you will get hurt.

265
00:18:55,428 --> 00:18:56,958
Hey, move, I am busy.

266
00:19:00,058 --> 00:19:01,568
What? Let go.

267
00:19:01,628 --> 00:19:04,438
Please let my old skills come back.

268
00:19:06,398 --> 00:19:07,408
Darn it.

269
00:19:10,878 --> 00:19:13,538
Man. I swear, darn it.

270
00:19:51,448 --> 00:19:53,448
(Police)

271
00:19:56,718 --> 00:20:00,458
You are truly amazing. And with your bare hands, too.

272
00:20:00,528 --> 00:20:02,328
It was not me...

273
00:20:02,388 --> 00:20:03,388
it was her.

274
00:20:04,498 --> 00:20:06,758
You must have done some martial arts.

275
00:20:06,828 --> 00:20:07,828
Well,

276
00:20:07,898 --> 00:20:09,528
a little bit of Hapkido and Taekwondo.

277
00:20:09,598 --> 00:20:10,898
Um Tae Bong, you too,

278
00:20:10,968 --> 00:20:13,738
caught a bad guy all by yourself before.

279
00:20:13,798 --> 00:20:15,908
I have been a huge fan since then.

280
00:20:17,108 --> 00:20:18,338
- Yes.
- Well, I'll be going now.

281
00:20:20,408 --> 00:20:21,448
Let us go.

282
00:20:31,118 --> 00:20:33,318
Did you catch a bad guy before, too?

283
00:20:33,388 --> 00:20:34,388
All by yourself?

284
00:20:35,958 --> 00:20:37,798
That is pretty cool.

285
00:20:37,858 --> 00:20:39,898
Why are you so eager to protect people?

286
00:20:39,958 --> 00:20:41,828
Fearlessly jumping in all the time.

287
00:20:41,898 --> 00:20:44,198
It is an occupational hazard. Why?

288
00:20:44,268 --> 00:20:46,438
Keep up the good work...

289
00:20:46,498 --> 00:20:48,368
and let us never cross paths again.

290
00:20:50,778 --> 00:20:53,838
Wow. Why the sudden temper?

291
00:20:56,778 --> 00:20:58,278
Goodbye,

292
00:20:58,348 --> 00:20:59,378
Han Jung Woo.

293
00:21:06,488 --> 00:21:08,228
(No Caller ID)

294
00:21:11,028 --> 00:21:12,028
Hello.

295
00:21:12,098 --> 00:21:15,568
You still love playing the hero, just like the old days.

296
00:21:15,628 --> 00:21:18,738
- Who are you?
- Well,

297
00:21:18,798 --> 00:21:20,968
- who could I be?
- Was it you?

298
00:21:21,038 --> 00:21:22,108
In the underground parking lot.

299
00:21:23,338 --> 00:21:25,838
- Who on earth are you?
- Um Tae Bong.

300
00:21:25,908 --> 00:21:27,548
We will meet again soon.

301
00:21:33,048 --> 00:21:34,548
That area is a blind spot for the security cameras,

302
00:21:34,618 --> 00:21:36,688
so it is hard to identify a suspect,

303
00:21:36,748 --> 00:21:38,188
and we did not find any fingerprints on the brick.

304
00:21:39,758 --> 00:21:41,758
Yes, I understand. Then,

305
00:21:41,828 --> 00:21:43,828
please contact me if you find anything.

306
00:21:47,768 --> 00:21:51,468
Do you really not remember his face? Hey, he altered his voice,

307
00:21:51,538 --> 00:21:54,138
and it means he was watching you earlier.

308
00:21:54,208 --> 00:21:55,268
Hey, do not worry.

309
00:21:56,368 --> 00:22:00,708
For now, I will make a list of guys...

310
00:22:00,778 --> 00:22:02,248
who might hold a grudge against you.

311
00:22:02,308 --> 00:22:05,818
First, Go Tae Sik, who lost the lead role to you last year.

312
00:22:05,878 --> 00:22:07,018
I heard his family is struggling,

313
00:22:07,078 --> 00:22:08,418
so he tried to get a big paycheck at once,

314
00:22:08,488 --> 00:22:11,118
but it fell through because of you. Do you think he holds a grudge?

315
00:22:11,188 --> 00:22:12,888
It is not him. Because of my bad rumours,

316
00:22:12,958 --> 00:22:14,358
he got the role in the movie I was fired from.

317
00:22:14,428 --> 00:22:15,428
That is right.

318
00:22:15,488 --> 00:22:18,798
Some jerk spread rumours that Um Tae Bong has a terrible temper.

319
00:22:18,858 --> 00:22:21,298
How did you know that? Were you that jerk?

320
00:22:21,368 --> 00:22:23,268
To get him that role?

321
00:22:23,328 --> 00:22:25,798
Hey, do you know how much the pay was?

322
00:22:25,868 --> 00:22:27,038
You are unbelievable.

323
00:22:28,608 --> 00:22:31,078
Or maybe her, the one who got famous from fake dating you...

324
00:22:31,138 --> 00:22:32,408
but lost popularity after you dumped her.

325
00:22:32,478 --> 00:22:34,978
What was her name again? Ms. P.

326
00:22:35,048 --> 00:22:36,448
Or Director Kim,

327
00:22:36,448 --> 00:22:38,948
who takes blood pressure pills because of you.

328
00:22:39,018 --> 00:22:42,518
He used to be very successful. His works had a lot of catchphrases.

329
00:22:42,588 --> 00:22:46,258
"I am a pushover." You probably do not know.

330
00:22:46,318 --> 00:22:48,428
I think he married the actress from that project.

331
00:22:48,488 --> 00:22:49,488
And now, a man like him...

332
00:22:49,558 --> 00:22:50,928
is taking blood pressure medication because of you.

333
00:22:50,998 --> 00:22:52,358
Or recently,

334
00:22:52,428 --> 00:22:53,898
Na Ri. After the dating rumours with you,

335
00:22:53,958 --> 00:22:55,868
she lost a lot of her older male fans.

336
00:22:55,928 --> 00:22:57,868
How long do we have to do this? All night?

337
00:22:57,938 --> 00:22:59,468
Then I should have brought my pyjamas.

338
00:22:59,538 --> 00:23:02,108
If you had behaved better, would this list be endless?

339
00:23:03,908 --> 00:23:06,178
Anyway, if he managed to find out your number,

340
00:23:06,238 --> 00:23:09,208
he is a very scary guy. First, change your number.

341
00:23:09,278 --> 00:23:14,088
No, they will definitely call again. If I want to track this jerk down,

342
00:23:14,148 --> 00:23:15,248
this is the only way.

343
00:23:15,318 --> 00:23:17,048
Hey, are you just going to sit back and wait for a call?

344
00:23:17,118 --> 00:23:20,258
Do not answer that unknown number again when you are alone.

345
00:23:20,318 --> 00:23:21,888
Tae Bong,

346
00:23:21,958 --> 00:23:23,428
let us get you a bodyguard.

347
00:23:24,428 --> 00:23:25,898
Darn it.

348
00:23:25,958 --> 00:23:28,328
- Are you saying that again?
- I mean,

349
00:23:29,528 --> 00:23:32,468
we should get you a secret bodyguard.

350
00:23:32,538 --> 00:23:34,568
A secret...

351
00:23:34,638 --> 00:23:35,668
bodyguard?

352
00:23:37,708 --> 00:23:39,808
Why are you so desperate to protect people?

353
00:23:41,178 --> 00:23:44,418
His temper has gotten even worse.

354
00:23:45,648 --> 00:23:48,018
I do not know why I am like this either.

355
00:23:52,088 --> 00:23:55,188
What? His back looks a lot like Jung Woo.

356
00:23:57,128 --> 00:23:59,298
- What?
- Hey.

357
00:24:01,698 --> 00:24:02,998
We ended up having dinner together.

358
00:24:07,738 --> 00:24:09,768
I was actually thinking about you earlier.

359
00:24:09,838 --> 00:24:12,708
But then you appeared right in front of me.

360
00:24:14,008 --> 00:24:15,708
My heart almost stopped.

361
00:24:26,158 --> 00:24:28,258
- It is spicy.
- Is it spicy?

362
00:24:29,628 --> 00:24:32,198
Should I not have bought it? I just missed this taste.

363
00:24:38,538 --> 00:24:41,368
I really thought my tongue was burning.

364
00:24:41,438 --> 00:24:44,278
This is strange. I am a huge fan of tteokbokki,

365
00:24:44,338 --> 00:24:46,008
so why does it feel like I am eating it for the first time?

366
00:24:47,578 --> 00:24:49,278
By the way,

367
00:24:49,348 --> 00:24:50,948
are you really the person in the room next to mine?

368
00:24:53,418 --> 00:24:54,718
Yes, why?

369
00:24:55,918 --> 00:24:57,048
Because I am so happy.

370
00:24:59,588 --> 00:25:00,588
Could it be...

371
00:25:01,758 --> 00:25:02,988
as much as me?

372
00:25:09,198 --> 00:25:10,198
Hurry up and eat.

373
00:25:51,908 --> 00:25:52,908
Who...

374
00:25:53,978 --> 00:25:55,148
are you exactly?

375
00:26:05,518 --> 00:26:06,518
Good luck.

376
00:26:12,158 --> 00:26:14,228
(Part-Time Worker Wanted, Hours Negotiable, Feel Free To Inquire)

377
00:26:15,698 --> 00:26:17,328
Excuse me.

378
00:26:17,398 --> 00:26:19,068
- Are you the owner?
- Yes.

379
00:26:19,068 --> 00:26:21,708
I'm Cha Hong Du. If you give me a task,

380
00:26:21,768 --> 00:26:23,038
I am confident I can do it well.

381
00:26:24,238 --> 00:26:26,938
These are my steel forearms built from part-time jobs.

382
00:26:27,008 --> 00:26:29,608
- What did you say?
- All I have is stamina and guts.

383
00:26:29,678 --> 00:26:30,918
I will be your best employee.

384
00:26:30,978 --> 00:26:32,018
It is okay, we already hired someone.

385
00:26:32,078 --> 00:26:33,078
We already found someone.

386
00:26:33,078 --> 00:26:34,488
I will be your best...

387
00:26:40,658 --> 00:26:42,558
Yes, I understand.

388
00:26:47,198 --> 00:26:48,228
It is Jung Woo.

389
00:26:51,438 --> 00:26:54,508
- Where are you going?
- I am going to work.

390
00:26:54,568 --> 00:26:55,638
But what are you doing here?

391
00:26:57,268 --> 00:27:00,008
Looking for a part-time job. But I have not found one yet.

392
00:27:01,678 --> 00:27:06,378
Oh, a bicycle. I am also good at...

393
00:27:07,548 --> 00:27:09,348
riding. Am I?

394
00:27:10,848 --> 00:27:13,258
Why do I not have any memory of riding a bicycle?

395
00:27:15,588 --> 00:27:17,458
Then...

396
00:27:17,528 --> 00:27:18,728
should I teach you?

397
00:27:20,028 --> 00:27:21,028
Really?

398
00:27:22,168 --> 00:27:23,928
I will see you at the park at three o'clock on Saturday.

399
00:27:26,038 --> 00:27:28,738
What? Really?

400
00:27:34,308 --> 00:27:37,878
Anyway. My stamina is terrible,

401
00:27:37,948 --> 00:27:41,388
my strength is terrible, and my kicks are terrible.

402
00:27:42,388 --> 00:27:44,588
Everything went down the drain in three years.

403
00:27:46,958 --> 00:27:49,958
Gosh, I have to pay rent, too.

404
00:27:50,028 --> 00:27:52,228
Should I blackmail that jerk with his secret?

405
00:27:55,398 --> 00:27:57,198
No, no.

406
00:27:57,268 --> 00:27:59,398
Let's not be that kind of pathetic person.

407
00:28:06,378 --> 00:28:08,108
Have we met before?

408
00:28:12,418 --> 00:28:14,688
He has changed a lot.

409
00:28:14,748 --> 00:28:16,318
Then again,

410
00:28:16,388 --> 00:28:18,918
his name is not even Han Jung Woo anymore,

411
00:28:18,988 --> 00:28:20,588
so his tastes must have changed, too.

412
00:28:24,828 --> 00:28:28,128
Why did he recommend someone like her?

413
00:28:28,198 --> 00:28:29,928
He said they would never see each other again.

414
00:28:34,508 --> 00:28:36,068
Come here and sit down.

415
00:28:36,138 --> 00:28:37,438
Here, right here.

416
00:28:47,748 --> 00:28:51,888
There is a saying in this world. Keep your enemies close...

417
00:28:51,958 --> 00:28:53,388
and keep those who might be your enemies...

418
00:28:53,458 --> 00:28:56,028
even closer.

419
00:28:56,088 --> 00:28:57,658
What are you talking about?

420
00:28:57,728 --> 00:28:59,428
Anyway,

421
00:28:59,498 --> 00:29:02,868
I saw you use your body quite well last time.

422
00:29:02,928 --> 00:29:04,798
Did you actually work out?

423
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:05,868
Yes, a little.

424
00:29:05,938 --> 00:29:07,338
Taekwondo rank 3 and Hapkido rank 2.

425
00:29:07,398 --> 00:29:09,638
Wow, you will not get beaten up with her around.

426
00:29:09,708 --> 00:29:14,138
Let us say someone has a secret. Like a weakness.

427
00:29:14,208 --> 00:29:15,848
What would you do if you found out about it?

428
00:29:18,678 --> 00:29:20,848
Would they give me money? How much would they give me?

429
00:29:22,018 --> 00:29:23,718
It depends on the amount.

430
00:29:25,458 --> 00:29:28,988
She has great capitalistic genes, right? She is my type.

431
00:29:29,058 --> 00:29:31,328
- We have a connection here.
- Last question.

432
00:29:31,398 --> 00:29:34,668
I will ask you directly. Do you like me?

433
00:29:37,528 --> 00:29:38,798
Have you completely lost your mind?

434
00:29:38,868 --> 00:29:41,738
Bravo. That is it. You pass.

435
00:29:43,768 --> 00:29:45,538
What are you doing after calling me all the way here?

436
00:29:45,608 --> 00:29:48,608
Passed with top honours. Now, right here.

437
00:29:48,678 --> 00:29:51,148
You just need to sign here.

438
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:52,778
(Contract)

439
00:29:52,848 --> 00:29:56,888
It is an employment contract. To hire you as my bodyguard.

440
00:29:56,948 --> 00:29:58,458
The pay is 2,300 dollars a month.

441
00:29:58,518 --> 00:30:02,188
You must accompany our actor Um Tae Bong on his schedule at all times.

442
00:30:02,258 --> 00:30:03,858
However,

443
00:30:03,928 --> 00:30:07,358
the fact that you are Tae Bong's bodyguard...

444
00:30:07,428 --> 00:30:09,468
is an absolute secret.

445
00:30:14,938 --> 00:30:15,968
One more thing.

446
00:30:18,038 --> 00:30:19,078
That night.

447
00:30:24,048 --> 00:30:26,618
Did you really not notice...

448
00:30:26,678 --> 00:30:28,418
anything strange about me?

449
00:30:35,588 --> 00:30:36,988
I did not.

450
00:30:37,058 --> 00:30:39,758
Of course you did not.

451
00:30:39,828 --> 00:30:44,738
But keep this in mind. The contract with me is an absolute secret.

452
00:30:44,798 --> 00:30:46,898
- I know.
- Do not forget.

453
00:30:46,968 --> 00:30:50,568
If you break it, you will pay a massive price.

454
00:30:50,638 --> 00:30:54,238
I get it, and if it is about protecting you,

455
00:30:54,308 --> 00:30:56,578
I will even risk my life.

456
00:30:56,648 --> 00:30:57,848
On that note...

457
00:30:59,178 --> 00:31:01,888
could you possibly give me some of the money in advance?

458
00:31:01,948 --> 00:31:05,488
Oh, of course, I knew you would say that,

459
00:31:05,558 --> 00:31:06,918
so I prepared a 50 percent advance.

460
00:31:06,988 --> 00:31:09,988
Here, take it. Your social security number...

461
00:31:10,058 --> 00:31:11,658
Hand over your ID card first.

462
00:31:11,728 --> 00:31:13,798
Because identity verification is required.

463
00:31:13,858 --> 00:31:15,298
My ID card?

464
00:31:17,268 --> 00:31:19,398
Well...

465
00:31:19,468 --> 00:31:22,138
I think I might have lost it, and this is...

466
00:31:22,208 --> 00:31:25,308
Then just the number, what is your number...

467
00:31:25,378 --> 00:31:27,838
My Social Security number is...

468
00:31:31,248 --> 00:31:32,918
(Cha Hong Du Life Record)

469
00:31:32,978 --> 00:31:34,988
(Date of Birth: 950704-29...)

470
00:31:35,048 --> 00:31:37,118
Ninety-five...

471
00:31:37,188 --> 00:31:38,888
What, 95?

472
00:31:38,958 --> 00:31:41,358
Someone born in 1995 has spoken informally to me this whole time?

473
00:31:41,428 --> 00:31:42,428
You.

474
00:31:42,488 --> 00:31:45,528
- Call me "sir" from now on.
- No.

475
00:31:45,598 --> 00:31:46,598
I've talked casually for so long...

476
00:31:46,658 --> 00:31:47,928
do you think I can change that overnight?

477
00:31:47,998 --> 00:31:49,398
When exactly did we...

478
00:31:51,538 --> 00:31:52,538
For a long time?

479
00:31:54,608 --> 00:31:56,338
Fine. Just sign it quickly.

480
00:32:00,938 --> 00:32:02,978
(Cha Hong Du)

481
00:32:10,818 --> 00:32:12,558
Keep this in mind.

482
00:32:12,618 --> 00:32:15,658
I have your face right here. If you breach the contract,

483
00:32:15,728 --> 00:32:17,388
I will broadcast it all over the country that very day.

484
00:32:17,458 --> 00:32:19,128
I get it, I get it.

485
00:32:19,128 --> 00:32:22,798
So, what should I do first?

486
00:32:24,428 --> 00:32:25,598
Do not tell me...

487
00:32:25,668 --> 00:32:28,538
you are going to be my bodyguard looking like that?

488
00:32:41,178 --> 00:32:43,648
- What is wrong with it?
- Are you filming Men in Black?

489
00:32:43,718 --> 00:32:44,718
Why?

490
00:32:44,788 --> 00:32:47,488
You might as well write "bodyguard" on your forehead.

491
00:32:47,558 --> 00:32:48,858
I saw at the market...

492
00:32:48,928 --> 00:32:50,588
they were selling hats that said "bodyguard."

493
00:32:50,658 --> 00:32:52,528
- Should I buy one and wear it?
- Hey.

494
00:32:54,398 --> 00:32:56,568
You are my secret bodyguard.

495
00:32:56,628 --> 00:32:58,598
Then what kind of clothes am I supposed to wear?

496
00:32:58,668 --> 00:32:59,668
Here,

497
00:32:59,738 --> 00:33:02,268
it is best to dress like this so it is not obvious you are a bodyguard.

498
00:33:02,338 --> 00:33:04,938
I will introduce you to people as the new stylist.

499
00:33:05,008 --> 00:33:06,878
- My assistant.
- Yes.

500
00:33:06,938 --> 00:33:08,578
He might seem a bit prickly on the outside,

501
00:33:08,648 --> 00:33:10,348
but on the inside...

502
00:33:10,408 --> 00:33:11,448
he is even more prickly.

503
00:33:11,518 --> 00:33:13,018
So it is going to be very difficult for you from now on.

504
00:33:13,078 --> 00:33:15,818
When he gets annoyed, just think about something else.

505
00:33:15,888 --> 00:33:19,458
- Then the time will fly by.
- Yes. I will work hard from now on.

506
00:33:21,118 --> 00:33:23,628
Do I pay your salary? Well, I work hard too.

507
00:33:23,688 --> 00:33:24,898
Change your clothes and come out.

508
00:33:28,828 --> 00:33:30,928
She is so cool.

509
00:33:30,998 --> 00:33:32,568
She is exactly my style.

510
00:33:42,508 --> 00:33:44,248
Hey, you, rookie.

511
00:33:45,948 --> 00:33:46,948
Come on.

512
00:33:51,388 --> 00:33:53,258
Are you...

513
00:33:53,318 --> 00:33:54,858
Are you really here as a bodyguard?

514
00:33:54,928 --> 00:33:56,788
I think so?

515
00:33:56,858 --> 00:33:58,728
You are not here as the new manager?

516
00:33:58,798 --> 00:34:00,258
I do not think so?

517
00:34:00,328 --> 00:34:03,098
Come on. Don't you know how to use honorifics?

518
00:34:03,168 --> 00:34:04,938
From now on, at the end of everything this senior says,

519
00:34:04,998 --> 00:34:08,038
you must always use honorifics. Got it?

520
00:34:08,108 --> 00:34:09,108
Got it.

521
00:34:11,038 --> 00:34:12,938
I understand, sir.

522
00:34:14,278 --> 00:34:16,208
Well, if you are a bodyguard, really...

523
00:34:16,278 --> 00:34:19,178
- Are you good at fighting?
- Taekwondo,

524
00:34:19,248 --> 00:34:21,988
Kendo, Judo.

525
00:34:23,248 --> 00:34:25,218
Oh, what else is there...

526
00:34:26,788 --> 00:34:27,788
Even so, kid.

527
00:34:27,858 --> 00:34:31,328
Experience is everything. You are at the bottom, got it?

528
00:34:31,398 --> 00:34:34,158
- I understand.
- That is right, "I understand."

529
00:34:34,228 --> 00:34:35,228
Let's go.

530
00:34:36,768 --> 00:34:38,468
He is...

531
00:34:39,638 --> 00:34:44,368
so honest. He is exactly my type, too.

532
00:34:45,438 --> 00:34:47,938
Hello. I am Cha Hong Du.

533
00:34:48,008 --> 00:34:49,948
- Look forward to working with you.
- Yes.

534
00:34:50,008 --> 00:34:52,748
She is our new youngest stylist. This is our director.

535
00:34:52,818 --> 00:34:54,578
His directing skills are the best in the industry.

536
00:34:54,648 --> 00:34:58,988
Oh, come on, not the best. But your name is Cha Hong Du?

537
00:34:59,058 --> 00:35:02,088
Then is your older sister Gil Ra Im, and your younger sister Dong Baek?

538
00:35:08,028 --> 00:35:09,128
No, they are not.

539
00:35:10,168 --> 00:35:11,398
Wait, but...

540
00:35:11,468 --> 00:35:13,198
Aren't you the one who barged onto the set last time...

541
00:35:13,268 --> 00:35:15,508
that fan of Um Star?

542
00:35:15,568 --> 00:35:17,008
Anyway,

543
00:35:17,068 --> 00:35:18,878
